    "description": "Delete Deal Version. The client scrapped it — what they wanted was an edit log.\n\n=== FIELDS ===\n\n* DELETE: Deal_Version__c\n\n=== IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS ===\n\n* Remove the field, and remove it from layouts, list views, RELATED-LIST COLUMNS (BUILD-132 — Kobi on Aug 17: 'there's no deal version. So that entire column can be removed'), reports, and any formula referencing it.\n\n* Joyce, Aug 11: 'Honestly, I thought I got that from you. Like, from the original screen. So I do not care about that. We can definitely scrap it.'\n\n* Do not close without BUILD-157 (field history tracking). That's the actual requirement Deal Version stood in for: 'as long as we have the edit log for who makes updates and stuff.'\n\n* No supersede / versioning behaviour survives. Any spec describing Deal supersede logic is stale — worth a sweep of the PRD and the integration design doc.\n\n=== NOTES ===\n\n* Kobi restated the original intent before agreeing to remove it: versioning existed so a closed Deal and a new Deal with an identical partner/operator/market/vertical combination could be told apart. If that ever bites, this is the decision that caused it.\n\n=== SOURCE ===\n\n* Aug 11 call — Joyce/Kobi 53:20-54:07\n\n* Aug 17 call — column removal\n\nDependencies: BUILD-157 is the replacement\n\nRemember to update the requirements documentation as part of this change.\n\nPolished 2026-08-17 from the Operator/Partner ticket review, approved by Kobi.",
